reconstructed research.md "Spike findings" (T018, 8.1.17: nodeConfig for all 20 allowlisted names) in the helper protocol (contracts/helper-protocol-delta.md "Frames", research D-2, D-10) as ClientHelper writes it for op=nodeConfig, request names=OperationMode,ClusterName,ZoneName,NodeName,LocalMaintenanceMode,ActivateClusterManager,ClusterDebug,ContainerShutdownOnNodeFailure,RegisterMBeans,RegisterInternalMBeans,RuntimeDataCacheXMXPercentage,socketTimeoutInMillisecs,indexEnabled,iterationCount,DataSourceLocation,LogsDBDataSourceLocation,RepositoryDataSourceLocation,ClusterBindAddress,noOfRetries,retryInterval.
The shape of the real answer: the 11 names T018 saw answered with their types, all editable true and deprecated false; the other 9 in the error form T018 saw for every one of them (config <name> error com.inubit.ibis.utils.InubitException with the internal INUBIT error wrapping Cannot invoke "Object.getClass()" because "o" is null, the answer for a property the node does not have). The DataSourceLocation value carries a credential-looking user=ibis;password=example-secret for the defence-in-depth masking (D-21), invented for it. Not recorded: written by hand with the fixed nonce of the 020/021 fixtures and the two log4j lines of fixtures/server-log/v8_1/webservice/ok.frames; all names and values are fictitious (node1, acme-cluster, java:/comp/env/jdbc/IBISDB, ibis, example-secret), the display names, categories and descriptions are invented. Formerly the reconstructed all case; kept beside the recorded all (T038) because it carries the credential-looking DataSourceLocation value for the D-21 masking.
